<!-- ══ COMMUNITY ══ -->
<section class="page" data-page="community">
  <section class="band">
    <span class="label">The Community</span>
    <h1 class="big" style="margin:1.5rem 0 1.75rem;max-width:22ch">Six homes, and everything they share.</h1>
    <p class="lede dim measure">Eleven lots in total — six for homes, five held communally. Nothing on the plan is speculative: every lot is drawn and measured. Lot 1 has sold; Lots 3, 7, 8, 9 and 10 are for sale. Chat with our design team for a turnkey home, or bring your own — we place no rules or restrictions on what you build.</p>
    <p class="lede dim measure" style="margin-top:1.25rem">We're offering the Ki to a small number of people able to own in this magical place, in a way that helps the people who already live here. Change is inevitable; without the incentive to exploit, it can work for everyone. Bali is close to a case study in what not to allow in the early stages of a destination going global.</p>

    <figure class="sitefig" style="max-width:52rem">
      <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Masterplan of the site: lots 1 and 3 on the beachfront, six residential lots behind them, and shared land given to the spa, community restaurant, pickleball courts, football pitch and staff housing.">
      <figcaption>The masterplan. Beach and sea to the north; the coast road runs along the southern edge.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="split" style="margin-top:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,3.5rem)">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">What is on the plan</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li><span class="k">Beachfront</span><span>Two lots — 3,170 m² and 2,780 m², each with a 300 m² villa</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Residential</span><span>Six lots — 1,150 m² to 1,300 m², each with a 140 m² villa</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Spa</span><span>635 m²</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Restaurant</span><span>625 m², shared by the community</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Pickleball</span><span>1,680 m² — four courts</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Football pitch</span><span>1,950 m²</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Staff housing</span><span>1,420 m²</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">The villas</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Understated, and built to disappear.</h2>
        <p class="dim">Our approach begins with the ocean's rhythm and reef topography: structures are sited to frame surf breaks, capture breezes and preserve indigenous vegetation.</p>
        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:1rem">Indoor-outdoor living is emphasised — deep overhangs, shaded patios and expansive glazing open onto surf decks that give access to the beach.</p>
        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:1rem">Sustainability is embedded throughout: passive ventilation, minimal site disturbance and community-scale social spaces ensure the resort is both respectful of place and designed to enhance the experience of waves, land and life.</p>
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li><span class="k">Setting</span><span>A beachfront setting of 2.7 hectares, directly in front of Suicides</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Ownership</span><span>Six private lots — no rental pool, no rooms sold around you</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Systems</span><span>Solar power and rainwater harvesting across the site</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Service</span><span>Kitchen, housekeeping and boat crew shared across the six households</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Workshop</span><span>The Quiver Workshop — board storage, repairs, maintenance and watercraft support</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">Membership</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="big">Chosen, not sold to.</h2>
        <p class="lede dim">With six households sharing one beach for decades, who joins matters more than how quickly they join. The process is deliberately slow.</p>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step"><div class="n">01</div><div><h3>A conversation</h3><p class="dim">An unhurried call about how you surf, how you travel and what you are actually looking for. No deck, no pressure.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step"><div class="n">02</div><div><h3>Three days on site</h3><p class="dim">Those who we feel share the spirit and values of the community are invited to spend three days with us — surfing the breaks, eating with the team, seeing the land.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step"><div class="n">03</div><div><h3>Lot selection</h3><p class="dim">You choose from the remaining lots, and the villa design is developed with you within the site's material and height guidelines.</p></div></div>
          <div class="step"><div class="n">04</div><div><h3>Ownership</h3><p class="dim">Title, build, and a place on the roster for boats, guides and staff from the day you arrive.</p></div></div>
        </div>
        <a class="link" href="#/enquire" style="margin-top:2.5rem">Begin at step one</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>

<!-- ══ SURF ══ -->
<section class="page" data-page="surf">
  <section class="band">
    <span class="label">Surf</span>
    <h1 class="big" style="margin:1.5rem 0 1.75rem;max-width:20ch">A surfer's nirvana, minus the negotiating.</h1>
    <p class="lede dim measure">The constraint in the Mentawais has never been waves. It is boats, crowds and other people's schedules. Ki removes all three: dedicated boats and experienced local guides, so owners reach the best wave for the conditions that day — at first light, at the tide, or not at all.</p>
    <div class="datum" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span><span class="label">Out front</span><b>SUICIDES</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Within range</span><b>10 BREAKS</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Boats</span><b>DEDICATED</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Guides</span><b>LOCAL</b></span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="bandphoto" style="background-image:var(--photo-surf)" role="img" aria-label="A surfer high on the face of a long, hollow blue wall, the lip throwing ahead of him down the reef."></div>

  <section class="band">
    <h2 class="mid">The ten.</h2>
    <p class="dim measure" style="margin-top:.9rem">Rights and lefts, beginner sandbars and freight-train barrels — inside a run short enough that the call can be made at breakfast and remade by lunch.</p>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table class="breaks">
        <thead><tr><th>Break</th><th>Hand</th><th>Level</th><th>Character</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Suicides<span class="alias">Ariks</span></td><td><span class="hand">R</span></td><td class="lvl">Advanced</td><td class="dim">The wave at the door. A high-octane, all-out freight-train barrel over reef — the reason the land was bought.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Telescopes<span class="alias">Tellies</span></td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Intermediate +</td><td class="dim">World class, and working somewhere in its length nearly all year. The one everyone else queues for.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Scarecrows</td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Intermediate +</td><td class="dim">An incredibly consistent left over reef. Rarely off, rarely a wasted trip out.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Tikus<span class="alias">The Rat</span></td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">All levels</td><td class="dim">Forgiving and soft-shouldered — perfect for beginners, and where the family ends up.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Icelands<span class="alias">The Ice</span></td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Intermediate +</td><td class="dim">Two completely different personas depending on size and tide. Worth reading before you paddle.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Ombak Tidur<span class="alias">The Sleeping Wave</span></td><td><span class="hand">R</span></td><td class="lvl">Intermediate +</td><td class="dim">Fast walls and the occasional pit. Wakes up with size.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>7 Palm<span class="alias">Ulars</span></td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Intermediate +</td><td class="dim">Rides that can stretch up to 200 yards. Legs first, arms second.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Twiggies</td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Advanced</td><td class="dim">A fun wave to explore, particularly when Telescopes feels crowded.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Hookers</td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">Advanced</td><td class="dim">Fast left-handers, complete with speed walls. Commit early.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>G-4</td><td><span class="hand L">L</span></td><td class="lvl">All levels</td><td class="dim">An uncrowded wave most camps don't even consider. Which is exactly the point.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">On land</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">The Quiver Workshop.</h2>
        <p class="dim">Board storage, repairs and maintenance on site, alongside support for the community's watercraft. Boards live here between trips; dings are fixed overnight rather than carried home.</p>
        <h2 class="mid" style="margin-top:2rem">If it goes wrong.</h2>
        <p class="dim">Ki sits on the only island in the Mentawais with a hospital, and owners have telehealth access to Dr. Montee. It is a long way from anywhere — which is the appeal, and the reason this matters.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</section>

<!-- ══ REJUVENATE ══ -->
<section class="page" data-page="rejuvenate">
  <section class="band">
    <span class="label">Rejuvenate</span>
    <h1 class="big" style="margin:1.5rem 0 1.75rem;max-width:20ch">Everything you need to get back in the water.</h1>
    <p class="lede dim measure">Recovery here is not an add-on for the people who don't surf. It is what makes a two-week trip a two-session-a-day trip — and it works just as well for partners and families who came for the island rather than the reef.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">The spa</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Salt, sun and shoulders.</h2>
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li><span class="k">Bodywork</span><span>Deep tissue massage aimed at post-surf tension — shoulders, lats, lower back</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Skin</span><span>Treatments built for constant sun and saltwater exposure, not city skin</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Package</span><span>Morning Waves &amp; Muscle Melt — dawn session, massage, skin treatment</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">For</span><span>Surfers, non-surfers, couples and families</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">The gym</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Surf-specific, not hotel-specific.</h2>
        <p class="dim">A fitness centre built around what surfing actually asks of a body — balance, rotation, and the ability to go again tomorrow.</p>
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li><span class="k">Movement</span><span>Balance boards and resistance training</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Technique</span><span>Video analysis — session footage reviewed and worked on</span></li>
