<!-- ══ OWNERSHIP ══ -->
<section class="page" data-page="ownership">
  <section class="band">
    <span class="label">Ownership</span>
    <h1 class="big" style="margin:1.5rem 0 1.75rem;max-width:20ch">Six homes. Never a seventh.</h1>
    <p class="lede dim measure">Ownership at Ki is a lot inside a community of only six villas in a beachfront setting, held through your own Indonesian company, with resort-caliber services attached. There is no rental pool and no rooms sold around you — the site only ever holds six households.</p>
    <div class="datum" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
      <span><span class="label">Total site</span><b>2.7 HECTARES</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Lots</span><b>6</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Setting</span><b>BEACHFRONT</b></span>
      <span><span class="label">Structure</span><b>HGB VIA PT PMA</b></span>
    </div>

    <figure class="sitefig">
      <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Aerial view of the site: the coast road curving along one edge, cleared ground and standing jungle, the coconut palm line and beach, and the reef breaking beyond.">
      <figcaption>The site as it stands — the coast road along one edge, the palm line and beach along the other, and the reef breaking beyond it.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Held through your own Indonesian company.</h2>
        <p class="dim">Your Indonesian foreign-investment company holds Hak Guna Bangunan (HGB), giving the company registered rights to build on and use the land. Indonesian authorities specifically recognize PT PMAs as able to obtain HGB for qualifying investment activities.</p>
        <ul class="ruled">
          <li><span class="k">Vehicle</span><span>PT PMA — an Indonesian foreign-investment company</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Land right</span><span>Hak Guna Bangunan (HGB) — registered rights to build on and use the land</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Held by</span><span>The company, rather than the individual</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Basis</span><span>Recognised for qualifying investment activities</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Set up by</span><span>Ki, with Indonesian counsel and notaries, as part of the purchase</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Run by</span><span>Ki — annual filings, reporting and renewals handled on your behalf</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Cost</span><span>Formation and the first year's compliance are included in the purchase</span></li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="mid" style="margin-top:1rem">And you don't have to run any of it.</h2>
        <p class="dim">None of this is left for you to work out. We form the company, register the land right and put the structure in place as part of the purchase, working with Indonesian counsel and notaries who have done it here before. Once it is running, we keep it in good standing — the annual filings, the reporting, the renewals — so what is asked of you is a signature where one is genuinely needed, and nothing else. Formation and the first year's compliance are included in the purchase, and everything beyond that is set out in full before you commit — there are no surprises afterwards.</p>
        <p class="note">A summary of the structure, not legal or tax advice. Your own counsel should review the arrangement before you commit to anything.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">Payment schedule</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Staged against the build, not against a calendar.</h2>
        <div class="tablewrap" style="max-width:34rem;width:100%">
          <table class="sched">
            <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Instalment</th><th>Paid to date</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Upon signing / exchange</td><td class="amt">20%</td><td class="cum">20%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Foundations &amp; structure complete</td><td class="amt">25%</td><td class="cum">45%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Building watertight / roof complete</td><td class="amt">25%</td><td class="cum">70%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Fit-out substantially complete</td><td class="amt">25%</td><td class="cum">95%</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Villa completed &amp; handed over</td><td class="amt">5%</td><td class="cum">100%</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Each instalment falls when the milestone is met, not on a fixed calendar date.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">Seller financing available</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">Flexibility in how the purchase is structured.</h2>
        <p class="dim">Seller financing is available for qualified purchasers, offering greater flexibility in how the purchase is structured.</p>
        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:1rem">Financing terms, deposit requirements and repayment periods are agreed individually with each purchaser.</p>
        <p class="dim" style="margin-top:1rem">Please enquire for current terms and availability.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band dark">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="stack tight"><span class="label">What comes with the land</span></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <h2 class="mid">A house, and a crew.</h2>
        <ul class="ruled" style="--line:var(--panel-line);--line-soft:var(--panel-line)">
          <li><span class="k">Water access</span><span>Dedicated boats and experienced local surf guides, on the day's conditions rather than a fixed schedule</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Quiver Workshop</span><span>Storage, repair and maintenance for boards and community watercraft</span></li>
          <li><span class="k">Wellness</span><span>Spa, surf-specific gym, cryochamber, sauna and ice bath</span></li>
